
<p>Verizon, in a post headlined “Switch to Verizon and Get the New iPhone Duo Now. No Trade-In Needed.”:</p>

<blockquote>
  <p>Verizon will support iPhone Handoff, giving customers the
flexibility to use a single Verizon phone number seamlessly
across two compatible iPhone models. Whether using the pocketable
iPhone Duo on the go or iPhone 18 Pro for work, customers can
switch active status between devices at any time while keeping
full access to Verizon’s 5G network. iPhone Handoff will be
available from Verizon for $10/month on compatible iPhones models
running iOS 27.</p>
</blockquote>

<p>First, the word “now” is <a href="https://daringfireball.net/linked/2026/10/18/apple-duo-shortage-statement">doing a lot of work</a> in that headline, given the current January 25 estimate for new Duo orders.</p>

<p>Second, we all know Verizon is the most expensive competent carrier in the U.S. (Maybe AT&amp;T is just as expensive, but I said “competent”.) It feels like a rip <a href="https://daringfireball.net/linked/2026/09/12/tmobile-iphone-handoff-price-gauging">that T-Mobile is charging $5/month</a>. Verizon charging double is on-brand but irritating.</p>

